# 7. 📦 COPY vs ADD

Both instructions can copy files into a Docker image.

## COPY

Preferred for normal file copying.

```dockerfile
COPY app.py /app/
```

## ADD

Provides additional functionality, such as extracting local tar archives.

```dockerfile
ADD app.tar.gz /app/
```

### Best Practice

For normal application files:

```dockerfile
COPY
```

> **Use `COPY` unless you specifically need an `ADD` feature.**

