# 10. 🐳 Important Docker Concepts

## Docker Image

An image contains everything required to run an application.

```text
Application
     +
Dependencies
     +
Libraries
     +
Configuration
     +
Base Image
     ↓
Docker Image
```

---

## Docker Container

A container is an isolated runtime environment created from an image.

```text
Docker Image
     ↓
Docker Container
     ↓
Application Running
```

---

## Docker Volume

A volume provides persistent storage outside the container's writable filesystem.

```text
Container
     │
     ↓
Docker Volume
     │
     ↓
Persistent Data
```

Commonly used for:

* MySQL
* PostgreSQL
* Redis
* Application data

---

## Docker Network

A Docker network allows containers to communicate.

```text
             Docker Network
                  │
        ┌─────────┴─────────┐
        ↓                   ↓
     Backend              Database
        │                   │
        └─────── db ────────┘
```

