# 21. 📂 Volume vs Bind Mount

| Feature              | Docker Volume  | Bind Mount              |
| -------------------- | -------------- | ----------------------- |
| Managed by Docker    | ✅ Yes          | ❌ No                    |
| Storage location     | Docker-managed | User-selected host path |
| Good for databases   | ✅ Yes          | Possible                |
| Good for development | Possible       | ✅ Excellent             |
| Example              | `mydata:/data` | `./app:/app`            |

### Volume

```bash
-v mydata:/data
```

### Bind Mount

```bash
-v $(pwd)/app:/app
```

### Easy Interview Answer

> **Volume is managed by Docker, while a bind mount maps a specific host filesystem path into the container.**

