# 22. 🎯 CMD vs ENTRYPOINT

This is one of your important weak areas.

## CMD

Provides the default command or arguments.

```dockerfile
CMD ["python", "app.py"]
```

It can easily be overridden when running the container.

## ENTRYPOINT

Defines the main executable of the container.

```dockerfile
ENTRYPOINT ["python"]
```

Then:

```bash
docker run my-image app.py
```

effectively runs:

```text
python app.py
```

### Simple Interview Explanation

> **ENTRYPOINT defines what the container primarily runs, while CMD provides default arguments or a default command that can be overridden.**

